		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=1781&amp;p=15382#p15382"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Would anyone have a schematic of the CH1801 charger.   My charger stays in the Charge mode.  Never switches from RED to GREEN<br>indicating CHARGE COMPLETE.  </div></blockquote>I have two of them that do <em class="text-italics">exactly</em> what you describe.  When new, they worked just fine. (charging overnight, would be GREEN by morning)<br>Then one of them stayed red all the time when radio in the charger.  THEN that charger stayed red all the time even when there was no radio in the charger.<br>Then, the 2nd one would show the GREEN, but very dimly.  Now, the 2nd one shows NO color, but will charge the radio just fine.<br><br>At this point, I have just grown to ignore it, leave both radios on most days until battery warning, then back in charger for 8-10 hours, and all good.  The batteries never get warm in the charger and have measured the charged battery at around 8.3 to 8.5 volts, which is 100 percent in my book and certainly 100 percent on the Open1801 indicators.<br><br>I don't think I'm gonna jack with it, but it's good to see someone has something to try for a repair or band-aid.<br><br>7-3 - N0GIK - Matt<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1896">n0gik</a> — Thu Jul 29, 2021 3:10 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
