		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=1781&amp;p=15371#p15371"><![CDATA[
Would anyone have a schematic of the CH1801 charger.   My charger stays in the Charge mode.  Never switches from RED to GREEN<br>indicating CHARGE COMPLETE.   It's been that way from day one but just assumed I never charged long enough.<br>Charging it for more than 10 hours still doesn't change.  The battery measures around 8.3 volts when removed<br>from the charger and seems to last a long time.   I tried tracing the etch and came up with something schematic wise<br>that is 99% the same as a what's called a SC6038.  The only difference is they run the EN pin through a 10K to the D.C<br>input instead of just connecting it directly to D.C. input. EN high turns the chip on.      Would appreciate anyones experience with<br>the CH1801 and if a schematic is available just in case I missed something.<br><br>Guessing it's the HXN-WS chip is bad.   Might try a TP5100 charger board in the near future.<br><br>Ken<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=594">n1kk</a> — Wed Jul 28, 2021 3:54 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
